Thanks for grabbing our security resource from EdgeIQ Labs. Here's what you need to know:

The #1 vulnerability we see across thousands of scans isn't outdated software or weak passwords \u2014 it's exposed configuration files that leak API keys, database credentials, and internal endpoints.

Quick wins you can do today:
1. Add .env, *.config, and credentials.json to your .gitignore
2. Rotate any API keys found in public repos immediately
3. Enable branch protection on main/master branches

If you want automated monitoring for these issues, our tools handle it at scale:
\u2192 DNS Firewall ($5/mo): https://edgeiqlabs.com/dnsfirewall/
\u2192 Phishing Analyzer Pro ($29/mo): https://edgeiqlabs.com/phish-analyzer/
\u2192 StatusPage ($9/mo): https://edgeiqlabs.com/statuspage/

Stay safe out there.

EdgeIQ Labs Support`;
      await fetch("https://api.resend.com/emails", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
          "Authorization": `Bearer ${env.RESEND_API_KEY}`,
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          from: "EdgeIQ Labs <support@edgeiqlabs.com>",
          to: [email],
          subject: "Your security checklist from EdgeIQ Labs",
          html: welcomeBody.replace(/\n/g, "<br>")
        })
      });
    }
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }), {
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" }
    });
  } catch (e) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: e.message }), {
      status: 500,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" }
    });
